<http://data.silknow.org/object/1efd8324-af5d-3c63-8a27-57d7d02e5578>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "This cream gauze panel was painted in China for export to Europe, although it is not clear exactly how it would have been used in a Western interior. It could have served as a coverlet or a decorative hanging. The neutral colour of the background is a common feature of painted export silks of this type but would not have been admired in China itself."@en , "Hanging of white gauze-weave silk, painted with flowers and birds."@en , "Hanging, gauze-weave silk, painted with flowers and birds, China, ca. 1864"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/afd87474-51a5-3adc-a05a-2348c3562842> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "This cream gauze panel was painted in China for export to Europe, although it is not clear exactly how it would have been used in a Western interior. It could have served as a coverlet or a decorative hanging. The neutral colour of the background is a common feature of painted export silks of this type but would not have been admired in China itself."@en , "Hanging, gauze-weave silk, painted with flowers and birds, China, ca. 1864"@en , "Hanging of white gauze-weave silk, painted with flowers and birds."@en ;
